\ headers_vectors.fam — a dev network's header chain for headers.fam
\ (docs/NODE.md, step 4), each verdict tabminer's own Chain::accept_headers
\ gave it.  Written by miner/src/fam_vectors.rs (`cargo test --lib
\ write_fam_vectors -- --ignored`); not to be edited.  Plain code, for
\ headers_test.fam (a program under the OS, after powinit): it counts the
\ checks in vpass and vfail.

: vx variable ;  : vy variable ;  : vpass variable ;  : vfail variable ;  : vn variable ;
: vinit  vx @ 0= if 100 lit alloc vx !  100 lit alloc vy ! then ;
: v!  begin dup while 1 lit - rot 2 lit pick 2 lit pick w! repeat 2drop ;
: vok  vn @ 1 lit + vn !  if vpass @ 1 lit + vpass ! else vfail @ 1 lit + vfail !  "headers_vectors: check " puts vn @ u. " failed" puts 0A lit putc then ;
: vnow variable ;  : vnow2 variable ;
\ vh ( code -- )  the header at vx, offered now, gets code.
: vh  vx @ vnow @ vnow2 @ hacc  dup rot = dup 0= if "  got " puts over . 0A lit putc then vok drop ;

